{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"`/image/` on iiif.wellcomecollection.org grew from about 2.3M to 6M requests a day from 2026-09-22, and DLCS returned 502 and 504 in bursts that fired `cloudfront-iiif-5xx-image` and `cloudfront-iiif-5xx-image-rate` most days, mostly overnight UTC.\n\n## Done\n\nwellcomecollection/platform-infrastructure#557 holds each source on the iiif WAF, applied to prod, stage and test, and is being merged as it stands:\n\n- A fleet asking only for `/full/640,/` with 2024 browser versions, and `Mozilla/5.0 (compatible; crawler)` on `/image/` and `/thumbs/`: rate limited.\n- A `/full/2048,/` harvester posing as Chrome without Accept-Language: rate limited.\n- The largest crawl, a script with generated browser and IE user agents, no Referer and no Sec-Fetch headers, about 80,000 requests an hour: blocked.\n- One curl address hitting `/search/` and `/text/` at up to 26 a second: held to 300 per address in five minutes.\n\nNeither `/image/` alarm has fired since the block went in on 2026-10-07 at 14:51 UTC. Daily `/image/` 5xx has been 0.01% to 0.05% since 2026-10-09, against 0.28% to 0.34% the week before. Requests reaching DLCS fell from 6.9M on 2026-10-05 to 2.7M on 2026-10-12, against 2.0M a day before the crawl. Digirati moved image server traffic onto an internal load balancer on 2026-10-08 at 10:21 UTC, taking it off the NAT path.\n\n## Still open\n\n- Something rendering works pages on wellcomecollection.org loads `info.json` with a real Referer: 39k requests an hour at 03:00 UTC on 2026-09-14, 168k on 2026-10-08, 116k on 2026-10-13. The iiif WAF can't tell it apart from readers, so I think it has to be stopped on the website.\n- DLCS can't serve some works, so every request for them fails. This is a data gap, not load. It covers works `b28652095` to `b28652502` on `/image/` and `/thumbs/` (`/thumbs/` 5xx was 434 on 2026-10-11 and 656 on 2026-10-12), plus `b11536196` and `b13228961` on 2026-10-08. For Digirati.\n- Ask Digirati whether SpecialServer can stop rendering requests the client has abandoned, and what causes the minute-long fast 502 spikes.\n- Watch for the no-referer script starting to send a Referer.\n","closed_by":{"login":"kenoir","id":953792,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk1Mzc5Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/953792?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenoir","html_url":"https://github.com/kenoir","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenoir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenoir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenoir/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenoir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenoir/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenoir/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenoir/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenoir/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenoir/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wellcomecollection/platform/issues/6741/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wellcomecollection/platform/issues/6741/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}